WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.930
Every time you stream, search, or ask an AI,

2
00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:05.330
you are renting a computer in a giant building.

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:09.880
Land, power, a building, chips, a network, and software.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.880
Rented out by the hour, or by contract.

5
00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:13.850
It is a huge business.

6
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:17.950
Cloud rental earns $558 billion a year, growing 55 percent.

7
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.390
About $2.49 trillion more is already signed, in backlog.

8
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:23.100
Now the bill.

9
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.580
Five companies spent $230.4 billion in one quarter.

10
00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:29.560
One gigawatt campus costs about $52.6 billion,

11
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:30.400
as an illustration.

12
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.360
Here is the catch.

13
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:34.360
Chips wear out in about six years.

14
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.100
At today's GPU cloud prices, a campus barely breaks even,

15
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:39.660
and borrowing makes it worse.

16
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.840
So who keeps the money?

17
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:42.860
Chip makers.

18
00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.140
NVIDIA's operating margin is 66 percent.

19
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.740
The big clouds make 36 to 39 percent.

20
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.020
GPU clouds, zero or less.

21
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.160
The question is not whether AI is real.

22
00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:54.360
It is whether revenue per

23
00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.740
gigawatt outruns depreciation and interest.
